/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Every laboratory protocol needs this calculation.
   - r is the radius from spindle to tube bottom in cm; rpm is the rotor speed; RCF is a multiple of g.
   - In SI units RCF = ω²r/g, where ω is angular speed in rad/s and r is in m.
   - A particle in the tube moves outward until the drag of the liquid balances the push of the field.
   - v is the settling speed in m/s; d is the particle diameter in m; Δρ is particle density minus liquid density in kg/m³; ω is the angular speed in rad/s; r is the radius in m; η is the liquid viscosity in Pa·s.
   - For serum, clotted blood is spun at about 1000–2000 × g for 10 min; on a rotor of 15 cm radius that is about 2400–3500 rpm (worked example 2).
*/
