/* book Worked example 2: Q: A serum protocol asks for 1500 × g. (a) What speed is needed on a swing-out rotor with r = 15 cm? (b) The same tubes are put in a small rotor with r = 7.5 cm at that speed. What RCF do they get?
   1. Rearrange RCF = 1.118 × 10⁻⁵ × r × (rpm)²: rpm = √(RCF / (1.118 × 10⁻⁵ × r)).
   2. 1.118 × 10⁻⁵ × 15 = 1.677 × 10⁻⁴; 1500 / 1.677 × 10⁻⁴ = 8.94 × 10⁶.
   3. rpm = √(8.94 × 10⁶) = 2990, so set about 3000 rpm.
   4. In the small rotor: RCF = 1.118 × 10⁻⁵ × 7.5 × (2990)² = 1.118 × 10⁻⁵ × 7.5 × 8.94 × 10⁶ = 750 × g, half the force, because the radius is half.
   Answer: (a) About 3000 rpm (2990 rpm) on the 15 cm rotor. (b) Only 750 × g on the 7.5 cm rotor, so the protocol must be set by RCF, not by rpm. */
